WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:11.211
"Why doesn't the princess have gravity?" The king paced back and forth.

2
00:00:11.212 --> 00:00:14.303
"My queen, this child can't be ours.

3
00:00:14.304 --> 00:00:18.800
Someone took our baby and gave us this light one instead!"

4
00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:22.197
"Don't be silly, dear," the queen said.

5
00:00:22.198 --> 00:00:26.064
"I think something else caused this problem."

6
00:00:26.065 --> 00:00:28.766
"What do you mean?" the king asked.

7
00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:33.302
"We didn't watch Ellen carefully at the baptism. And . . . "

8
00:00:33.303 --> 00:00:36.524
The queen cleared her throat.

9
00:00:36.525 --> 00:00:49.248
" Someone who was not invited got too close to

10
00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:52.275
her." "Aha!" The king slapped his

11
00:00:52.276 --> 00:00:57.309
forehead. "I get it. My sister put a spell on her!"

12
00:00:57.310 --> 00:01:02.470
"Exactly," the queen said sadly.

13
00:01:02.471 --> 00:01:05.846
*** Everyone did their best to watch the baby

14
00:01:05.847 --> 00:01:08.363
princess. But accidents kept

15
00:01:08.364 --> 00:01:13.938
happening. For example, one fine summer day, Nanny put her to

16
00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:22.738
sleep. She covered the princess with a blanket to hold her

17
00:01:22.739 --> 00:01:28.398
down. Later the queen entered the room. She didn't see the sleeping

18
00:01:28.399 --> 00:01:34.286
baby. "What a nice day!" the queen said. "I'll let in some fresh

19
00:01:34.287 --> 00:01:37.435
air." She opened a window and then hurried

20
00:01:37.436 --> 00:01:42.059
off. She didn't realize a magical fairy wind was blowing

21
00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:46.513
outside. It swirled around the window, waiting to do some

22
00:01:46.514 --> 00:01:50.709
mischief. As soon as the queen left, the fairy wind rushed

23
00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:59.848
in. It danced over to the bed and swept up

24
00:01:59.849 --> 00:02:03.581
Ellen. Then it blew back

25
00:02:03.582 --> 00:02:10.628
outside. The small baby floated on the breeze like a tiny flower

26
00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:16.754
seed. When Nanny returned, the baby was

27
00:02:16.755 --> 00:02:19.364
gone! Nanny tried to stay

28
00:02:19.365 --> 00:02:22.652
calm. "The queen probably took her," she

29
00:02:22.653 --> 00:02:25.431
thought. She ran to the queen's

30
00:02:25.432 --> 00:02:29.797
room. "Your Majesty, do you have Princess

31
00:02:29.798 --> 00:02:36.268
Ellen?" "No." The queen went pale. "Is she missing?"

32
00:02:36.269 --> 00:02:40.636
"I'm afraid so," Nanny said.

33
00:02:40.637 --> 00:02:44.254
The queen yelled for help.

34
00:02:44.255 --> 00:02:48.406
A moment later the palace was as busy as a beehive.

35
00:02:48.407 --> 00:03:05.440
Everyone buzzed about, searching for the missing baby.

36
00:03:05.441 --> 00:03:11.417
Finally a shout rang out. "I found her!" a servant cried.

37
00:03:11.418 --> 00:03:14.067
Everyone ran out to the garden.

38
00:03:14.068 --> 00:03:17.908
The baby lay under a rosebush, sound asleep.

39
00:03:17.909 --> 00:03:21.335
A thick blanket of rose petals covered her.

40
00:03:21.336 --> 00:03:29.796
The king and queen sobbed with relief.

41
00:03:29.797 --> 00:03:34.664
The noise woke up Ellen, who laughed and laughed.

42
00:03:34.665 --> 00:03:42.277
She kicked her tiny feet, spraying rose petals everywhere.

